WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:06.830
It was an impeccably choreographed event ...
... designed to showcase China's transformation

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:14.230
from an inward-looking farming-based society
to the economic giant it is today.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:19.519
The country's President Xi Jinping credited
40 years of what he termed "socialism with

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:24.789
Chinese characteristics" for lifting people
out of poverty ... and putting China on the

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:29.429
international stage.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:32.910
But that stage - now more than ever before
- is fraught with tension.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:37.680
In a thinly-veiled reference to his country's
months-long trade dispute with the United

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:45.329
States, Xi had this to say:
There is no textbook of rules to follow for

00:00:45.329 --> 00:00:48.390
the reforms and opening of China.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:53.239
A country with five thousand years of history
and civilisation and with a population of

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:56.440
more than 1.3 billion people.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.789
No one is in a position to dictate to the
Chinese people what should or shouldn't be

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:03.749
done.

00:01:03.749 --> 00:01:09.850
No one - not even, seemingly, the leader of
the most powerful economy in the world.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:15.180
This footage shows Xi Jinping having dinner
with US President Donald Trump at the G20

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.590
summit in Argentina earlier this month.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:24.740
The result was an agreement to a 90-day truce
in their trade conflict.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:29.930
But the arrest, since then of a top executive
at Chinese tech equipment giant Huawei has

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:34.159
left that truce on shakier ground than ever.

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:38.759
The tone coming from Beijing today - was defiant.

00:01:38.759 --> 00:05:34.870
China won't be pushed around.

